 until  kickoff here I'll be inside on the call  and uh it's it's crazy there's like a  buzz going on around the stadium and uh  almost just I think me like many fans  and like the players you just want to  get this game started now do they  tailgate over there  no well uh you know I'm sure you saw  that there's designated fan zones where  you're allowed to drink uh outside of  the stadiums you are not allowed to  drink inside the stadiums there's no  alcohol unless you're in VIP  um you know take that for what it's  worth but it's not quite the same  culture although one of the best things  of a World Cup though really is all the  you know these melting pots of all the  different fans partying and bongo drums  and all the rest of it uh the pressure  on the United States is what if you  could measure it  this generation of players I think has  been built up as one of our most  exciting yet but yet no matter what  happened the last four years no matter  the fact that we're the second youngest  team in the tournament this team will be  judged on what happens tonight fair or  not fair U.S teams are judged at a World  Cup not if you win these domestic  competitions this is when the eyes of  our nation comes and watches soccer like  we become soccer Nations for small  moments that's during the World Cup I  mean we had on Black Friday us England  our highest watch men's game ever on  national TV almost 19 million viewers we  peaked at this is when people watch and  this is where you bring people into our  soccer tent and we as Americans we're  pretty damn good at sports we're great  at the NFL basketball baseball we're not  the best in soccer and I think there's  an expectation that we start to catch up  if we can't beat Iran in a game that's a  one and done to advance to the round of  16 I think it's going to once again send  the message the message that we're still  a little ways off here did you play  against Mass C or Ronaldo  I did yeah uh Messi I I tried to get a  piece of his shirt at any time in the  game unreal man uh you know that for me  is one that I'll tell my kids I hope  they their kids tell their grandkids  like that that to me is the best player  to have ever played the game I don't  know what you think watching him Dan I  mean like his just skill set and how  he's so diminutive but yet just so the  guy delivers I would love to see him  lift his first World Cup here in Qatar  but how do you explain his greatness if  I look at him and and we have athletes  in all different sports where you go it  defies logic because there's there's  nothing that is impressive when you see  Messi but then you see what he does when  he's on a soccer field how do you  explain it  yeah he he just says that Supernatural  ability think about some of the best  athletes that we have had in our history  and Michael Jordan is a guy right that  he carries that presence when you  stepped on a field with him or stepped  on a court with Jordan I I Steve Nash is  a good one of my buddies and he talked  about you know when I when I say who was  better LeBron or Michael Jordan and he  just said Jordan carried this Aura when  he was on the court that you you knew he  was always capable of delivering the big  time play and we continually ask that of  Messi right and Messi with his backs  against the wall the other night they  Argentina needed a win to stay in the  tournament who scores the goal it's  messy he has one chances  it's one shot he he just has that that  ability no matter what the pressure  tight spaces he can always deliver and  continues to carry that pressure and  make it seem like it's nothing so he's  he's a goat man just it's just so  impressive uh Ronaldo did you play  against him  I I did not  um you know Ronaldo is I guess such a  big figure like Messi but so different  right I just think they're contrasting  in the way if you looked at the two of  them in the room and I think you said  hey who's who's the better athlete  everybody would say it's Ronaldo right  like Ronaldo is built like a figurine  he's like a sculpture he is two percent  body fat he's handsome he's you know  he's powerfully strong both feet he's he  can jump out of the building  um I have a lot of respect for Ronaldo  I'm still on the messy team and I know  you know people are normally in one camp  or another I think just I I like Messi  and that he can fit into any team I  think Ronaldo uh has to play in a  specific type of team to be successful  I'll uh leave you with this the Saudis  got rolls royces after beating Argentina  is that true  yeah that is true yeah  uh do other kinds of Saudis the Saudis  got Rolls-Royce I actually just heard  that um  Christian pulisic gave all of his  teammates a Cartier watch uh ahead of  this tournament  has kind of you know sometimes the star  player on the team does that and he made  a point of saying to the guys like this  is a this is a special thing I'm giving  my teammates this and we're gonna do  this together Greg burhalter the coach  gave him Tiffany bracelets I I know  what's the equivalent for the US guys  right like if we beat Iran or we make a  run for the quarter finals what are we  giving these guys like let's let's name  it now let's go let's go out there and  get a sponsor like is an All-American  Ford pickup truck maybe uh maybe I could  talk Tesla yeah my well I'm sponsored by  Mercedes maybe we could uh you know we  could hook them up it's unlike the  Saudis where they're giving out a  Rolls-Royce to you pretty good hey um  Stu thanks for joining us we appreciate  it and uh have fun  Dan appreciate it man that's uh Stu  Holden the Fox Sports lead analyst for  uh the World Cup on the call for the  must win match the Men's National Team  versus Iran live coverage starts at one  Eastern on Fox and right up to uh  kickoff at two Eastern

